{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358188-antlion-style-peach","id":1358188,"title":"Antlion Style [PEACH]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-01T07:35:59-08:00","id":1358188,"title":"Antlion Style [PEACH]","content":"<b>Weapons</b><b>: </b>Antlion Style can be practiced unarmed, with one or two handed axes and hammers, or with a shield.<br /> <b>Armor</b><b>: </b>Antlion Style can be practiced in any kind of armor.<br /> <b>Other Abilities</b><b>: </b>Antlion Style relies on skill in crafting, generally something along the lines of Architecture, Carpentry, Masonry or similar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Working Under Fire</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>3m; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> This charm allows you to craft rudimentary barricades in a single turn. This is basically a take cover action rolled with (str+craft), except that it relies less on available cover and more on having some form of material to make cover out of. This is considered a basic project. If you later leave the cover, you may return to it with a take cover action without needing to roll.<br /> This barricade is designed to be temporary, and will fall apart fairly quickly after the fight is over. However, if you take time after the fight to improve it, or use a charm that more generally reduces crafting time alongside this (Such as Craftsman Needs No Tools), it will be a fully functional barricade.<br /> Mastery: This may be flurried with any action but an attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Ground-Breaking Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>4m; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> This supplements any form of attack. If it deals any decisive damage, or at least (defender\u2019s stamina) withering damage, the enemy is knocked back a range band. If they are, the space between you and them is considered difficult terrain for them.<br /> If the attack is a smashing attack, the smashing knocks them prone in addition to knocking them back a range band.<br /> <br /> <b>Instant Renovation Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>2m; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b><br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Working Under Fire<br /> Use this only on your turn, while in cover. An ally of your choice may reflexively take cover behind the same cover as you. If you made the cover, they gain (your craft) non-charm dice.<br /> <br /> <b>Antlion Form</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>8m; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b><br /> The martial artist uses their knowledge of creation to identify weaknesses in their enemy\u2019s defenses, and avoid any in their own. Increase the overwhelming of your weapons by 2. While in cover, ignore the first point of penalties to your defense, and increase your soak by 2. In heavy cover, double both of these.<br /> <br /> <b>Sinking Pit Kata</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>2m; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b><br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Antlion Form<br /> Walls serve to constrain the enemy, both in their strikes and their movement. As an enemy flees the martial artist builds the walls needed to constrain their motion.<br /> Use when called to oppose an enemy\u2019s movement action such as a rush or disengage. You may roll with (str+craft). If you succeed, they suffer a -2 penalty on all movement actions until the next time they successfully move, and may consider this a successful basic project.<br /> <br /> <b>Cunning Demolition Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>3m, 3i; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>Terrestrial, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Sinking Pit Kata<br /> While fortifications are a tool to defend, any good workman knows that there a times you must use a tool outside of its intended purpose.<br /> Use only while in cover. The cover collapses, rendering it unuseable as cover (If you are in cover behind a very large obstruction, only a section out to close range around you collapse). All enemies within must roll (dex+dodge) or (sta+resistance) against an environmental hazard of difficulty (your craft), with a damage of 3 for light cover, 5 for heavy cover, and 7 for full cover.<br /> Mastery: Increase the difficulty of the roll by (essence)<br /> Terrestrial: Only a single enemy suffers the hazard.<br /> <br /> <b>Four Walls Posture</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>2m; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Antlion Form<br /> You may flurry a full defense action as if you had a shield, and ignore the initiative cost. If you have a shield, you additionally ignore the defense penalty<br /> Mastery: You may flurry a full defense action with an attack, or with any simple charm of this style<br /> <br /> <b>Devouring Caught Prey </b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>3m (+1wp); <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Four Walls Posture<br /> You hound an enemy, driving them through an endless maze of walls. Make a withering attack, ignoring any defense bonuses for cover, including cover you are in. If, by the end of their next turn, they haven\u2019t moved at least one range band, you may pay a 1 willpower surcharge to make a reflexive decisive attack against them with the same bonuses.<br /> <br /> <b>Crushing Vice Prison</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>3m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>Decisive-Only, Terrestrial, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Cunning Demolition Method, Devouring Caught Prey <br /> A fortress and a prison differ only in which side the locks are on, a bodyguard and a warden only in who pays them. The stylists builds some binding or prison on their enemy. <br /> Make a difficulty 4 gambit with (Str+Craft). They have a -1 penalty on all actions, rising to -3 for movement actions, and lose 1i a turn into a special pool. Every time they miss with an attack, they lose another 1i into the pool.<br /> You may at any point make a special decisive attack whose damage is (pool\u2019s initiative+your craft) rather than your initiative. On a hit, rather than resetting you to base initiative, the effects of this gambit ends. If this incapacitates the enemy, or raises their wound level by at least 2 ranks, this counts as completing a major craft project.<br /> Terrestrial: The martial artist cannot make the special decisive attack. Don\u2019t bother recording how much initiative the pool gains.<br /> Mastery: When you make the special decisive attack, you may add your own initiative to the damage. If you do, reset to base initiative on a hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T14:26:47-08:00","id":1358254,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, and the charms fit together nicely.<br /> <br /> My only real complaints are that you've got a bit of unintended side effects and have gotten natural language everywhere.<br /> - Working Under Fire doesn't specify what type of cover it creates. <br /> - Working Under Fire's Mastery effect as written permits it to flurry with things that don't flurry, like other Simple charms. <br /> - Ground-Breaking Strike could have the 3rd sentence folded into the 2nd, &quot;...back a range band and the space between...&quot;. There's also ambiguity as to the interaction with Smashing, what happens if the Smashing option selected was knockback, do they go back two bands and prone? <br /> - Instant Renovation Prana needs to specify what they get the dice to. <br /> - Is the lack of a Reflexive activation method for Antlion Form intentional? <br /> - Sinking Pit Kata, &quot;... or disengage. You may oppose their roll with (Strength+Craft) instead of your normal pool. If you do so and succeed...&quot;<br /> - Cunning Demolition Method capital-N Needs to require a roll to destroy things you didn't make. Otherwise any random ESS2 asshole can obliterate anything they can hide behind. <br /> - Four Walls Posture, &quot;...flurry a Full Defense action as though your weapon had the Shield tag and ignore the Initiative cost. If your weapon has the Shield tag...&quot;. <br /> - Crushing Vice Prison, &quot;...with (Strength+Craft). If it succeeds, the target suffers a...&quot;. Additionally, &quot;at any time&quot; leaves me confused as to if you can make the special decisive out of turn and if it takes actions to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:25:37-08:00","id":1358320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358188-antlion-style-peach?p=1358254#post1358254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea, and the charms fit together nicely.<br /> <br /> My only real complaints are that you've got a bit of unintended side effects and have gotten natural language everywhere.<br /> - Working Under Fire doesn't specify what type of cover it creates.<br /> - Working Under Fire's Mastery effect as written permits it to flurry with things that don't flurry, like other Simple charms.<br /> - Ground-Breaking Strike could have the 3rd sentence folded into the 2nd, &quot;...back a range band and the space between...&quot;. There's also ambiguity as to the interaction with Smashing, what happens if the Smashing option selected was knockback, do they go back two bands and prone?<br /> - Instant Renovation Prana needs to specify what they get the dice to.<br /> - Is the lack of a Reflexive activation method for Antlion Form intentional?<br /> - Sinking Pit Kata, &quot;... or disengage. You may oppose their roll with (Strength+Craft) instead of your normal pool. If you do so and succeed...&quot;<br /> - Cunning Demolition Method capital-N Needs to require a roll to destroy things you didn't make. Otherwise any random ESS2 asshole can obliterate anything they can hide behind.<br /> - Four Walls Posture, &quot;...flurry a Full Defense action as though your weapon had the Shield tag and ignore the Initiative cost. If your weapon has the Shield tag...&quot;.<br /> - Crushing Vice Prison, &quot;...with (Strength+Craft). If it succeeds, the target suffers a...&quot;. Additionally, &quot;at any time&quot; leaves me confused as to if you can make the special decisive out of turn and if it takes actions to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your commentary.<br /> <br /> I was imagining Working Under Fire making cover proportional to how much you have in the way of materials, though probably not total.<br /> Ground-Breaking Strike is intended to require/assume you use the smashing attack to knock them prone, I don't think it should allow knocking someone back two range bands.<br /> The dice from instant renovation prana are to the roll to take cover.<br /> Antlion Form should have a reflexive activation condition, I just hadn't thought of one. Probably when you take cover, or make a successful craft roll.<br /> The special attack from Crushing Vice Prison is meant to happen any time you could make a decisive attack. It probably should specifically require an attack action since I don't want to figure out what happens if you use a charm that divides your initiative between decisive attacks or makes a decisive attack not using your initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T13:19:53-08:00","id":1358474,"title":"","content":"I like it - Got any Fluff to precede the mechanics? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T02:38:02-08:00","id":1358803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358188-antlion-style-peach?p=1358320#post1358320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antlion Form should have a reflexive activation condition, I just hadn't thought of one. Probably when you take cover, or make a successful craft roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with something like &quot;If the martial artist goes 3 rounds without moving into a new range band, they may reflexively activate Antlion Form.&quot; After all, the Antlion sits and waits for his prey to come to him. He doesn't go out and pursue them. <br /> <br /> On a related note, Sinking Pit Kata shouldn't work on Rushes, just opposing Disengage. Once you approach the Antlion, it's difficult to escape. <br /> <br /> As for the rest, my immediate thought is that the various (Strength + Craft) rolls should be changed. Instead of outright replacing the normal rolls for Take Cover, opposing Disengage, etc., these effects should enhance the normal versions. Perhaps giving bonus dice if you have an appropriate Craft. Doing that would make these Charms feel more like Martial Arts Charms rather than Craft Charms with combat effects. They should be flavored more around the martial artist expertly kicking up or knocking down some debris to enhance the action, rather than primarily using their craftsmanship. Alternatively the bonus can be based on the environment (how difficult the terrain is, for example). Since prepared fortifications count as difficult terrain, this would encourage th Antlion stylist to fight on ground they've prepared for combat, which would be thematically appropriate. I love the idea of a style that's all about preparation and bringing your enemies to where you have a home field advantage.<br /> <br /> Though now that I said that, Combat Craft charms would be cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T21:13:53-08:00","id":1359204,"title":"","content":"While mulling over a different martial arts style, I had a thought that might apply here, depending on your intent for these charms. Basically, if you want to keep the reliance on Craft rolls, have you considered making these Evocations for an Artifact hammer instead? Obviously that would limit its usage to just the character using the hammer. So that route would be better for if you intend this for just one character, rather than a whole school of martial artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}